THE POOL — 39 cards ship in the base set:
  Class trinkets (0 energy, Trinket, any number per deck):
    Archer, Warrior, Mage — each levels up its class.
  ARCHER (12): Sniper 2 (2/1 ranged), Sharpshooter 3 (3/1
    ranged + ping 1), Ambusher 3 (2/2 hidden), Assassin 6
    (5/1 hidden + stab 2), Bolt 1 (2 to a hero), Reload 2
    (repeat a minion/trinket's printed rules), Overcharge 3
    (choose: 1+1 or 3+3+3-to-self), Explode 3 (destroy own
    minion, deal its power), Hail of Arrows 3 (1 to all
    enemy minions), Wildfire 6 (trinket: 1 to ALL minions
    and ALL heroes each turn), Post 1 (trinket, lasts 2:
    cheap Archer minions enter ready + a copy), Gift 3.
  WARRIOR (10): Footsoldier 1 (1/2), Bear 2 (3/2), Tactician
    2 (1/2, -1 power to a target), Swords 2 (+power to all
    your minions), Shields 1 (+toughness to all), Duel 2
    (+1/+1, strip ranged, fight), Banner 3 (trinket),
    Pillage 4, Commander 5 (2/3), Rally 5.
  MAGE (11 + 3 tokens): Bouncer 1 (1/1, bounce on entry),
    Study 2 (draw 2, discard 2), Bubble Shield 2, Spirit 3
    (1/3), Plan 3 (trinket: draw now and next turn),
    Morphosis Chamber 3 (trinket), Overwork 3 (trinket),
    Burnout 0 (trinket), Oozification 4 (destroy a minion;
    its controller gets Oozes equal to its toughness),
    Control 5 (steal a minion), Summon Primordial 8
    (summons Primordial, 10/10). Tokens (not deckable):
    Ooze 0 (0/1), Primordial 10 (10/10), Bubble 0 (trinket).

CONSTRUCTION — the space's shape:
  Exactly 40 cards; 1-4 copies of any base card; class
  trinkets unlimited. Class chosen at setup (3 classes).
  Off-class cards cost +3 energy, reduced 1 per level of
  that class you hold (trinkets in play level you up) — so
  the splash region is priced, not forbidden, and a deck's
  class-level trajectory is part of its character. A hero
  at 0 life, or drawing from an empty deck, is out. 2-7
  heroes; classes are PUBLIC (playerClass(p)) — a bot may
  condition on the field's classes in real time, an axis
  no participant we have met uses yet.

REGIONS SAMPLED vs UNEXPLORED (TLUF):
  True: the four bundled precons are the only stock decks;
  veterans play customs from the same 39 (Burnout and Gift
  in traces prove Mage/Archer customs in the field).
  Unknown: every custom composition region — deckbuilding
  proper (copy counts, trinket counts, splash ratios) is
  untouched by our lineage; all our variants run precon
  decks verbatim. The RPS class cycle (Round 10's mapping
  legs) prices the class axis at stock level only.
  Fiction: games/cac/cards.md names cards that do NOT ship
  (Positioning, Trap, Formation, Poacher, the Mastery cycle,
  Archery Instructor, Swordmaster, Scholar, a neutral
  Minion) — design notes, not playable cards; filed as X2
  so no future round tunes against ghosts.

